# ============================================================
# 5) PRACTICE TASKS — 3 PER SHIFT
# ============================================================
# The scenario gates explicitly test Variables, Conditionals,
# and Loops. Three tasks per shift gives the gate the same
# three-success progression described by the scenario.
#
# Each task contains 2 test cases.
# Total:
#   3 shifts
#   9 practice tasks
#   18 test cases
#
# TestCaseId is left as 0 because it is database-generated.
# The AddPracticeTask endpoint accepts TestCases directly.


# -------------------------
# SHIFT 1 — VARIABLES
# -------------------------

### Practice 1.1 — Store coffee price
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/practice/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shiftId": {{shift1Id}},
  "taskOrder": 1,
  "title": "Store Coffee Price",
  "description": "Create an integer variable named coffeePrice and print it.",
  "starterCode": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    // Write your solution here\n    return 0;\n}",
  "conceptTag": "Variables",
  "difficulty": "SpacedRetrieval",
  "maxAttempts": 0,
  "egpReward": 20,
  "testCases": [
    {
      "testCaseId": 0,
      "taskId": null,
      "sideTaskId": null,
      "testInput": "",
      "expectedOutput": "Coffee - 45 EGP",
      "isHidden": false,
      "description": "coffeePrice should be 45."
    },
    {
      "testCaseId": 0,
      "taskId": null,
      "sideTaskId": null,
      "testInput": "",
      "expectedOutput": "Coffee - 40 EGP",
      "isHidden": true,
      "description": "Changing the variable value should change the printed result."
    }
  ]
}

###

### Practice 1.2 — Multiple menu prices
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/practice/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shiftId": {{shift1Id}},
